{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Embedding Models \u2014 The 2026 Deep Dive Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: baseline \u2014 dense embeddings with Sentence-BERT"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from sentence_transformers import SentenceTransformer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "encoder = SentenceTransformer(\"BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "corpus = ["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"The first iPhone launched in 2007.\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"Apple released the iPod in 2001.\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"Android is an operating system from Google.\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "emb = encoder.encode(corpus, normalize_embeddings=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "query = \"When was the iPhone released?\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "q_emb = encoder.encode([query], normalize_embeddings=True)[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "scores = emb @ q_emb"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(sorted(enumerate(scores), key=lambda x: -x[1]))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`normalize_embeddings=True` makes the dot product equal cosine similarity. Always set it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Matryoshka truncation"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def truncate(vectors, dim):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    out = vectors[:, :dim]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return out / np.linalg.norm(out, axis=1, keepdims=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "emb_256 = truncate(emb, 256)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "emb_128 = truncate(emb, 128)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Re-normalize after truncation. Nomic v1.5, OpenAI text-3, and Voyage-4 are trained so this is lossless for the first few levels. Non-Matryoshka models (original Sentence-BERT) degrade sharply when truncated."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: BGE-M3 multi-functionality"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from FlagEmbedding import BGEM3FlagModel"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "model = BGEM3FlagModel(\"BAAI/bge-m3\", use_fp16=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "output = model.encode("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    corpus,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return_dense=True,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return_sparse=True,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return_colbert_vecs=True,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# output[\"dense_vecs\"]:    (n_docs, 1024)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# output[\"lexical_weights\"]: list of dict {token_id: weight}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# output[\"colbert_vecs\"]:  list of (n_tokens, 1024) arrays"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Three indexes, one inference call. Score fusion:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "dense_score = ... # cosine over dense_vecs"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "sparse_score = model.compute_lexical_matching_score(q_lex, d_lex)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "colbert_score = model.colbert_score(q_col, d_col)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "final = 0.4 * dense_score + 0.2 * sparse_score + 0.4 * colbert_score"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Tune the weights on your domain."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: MTEB eval on a custom task"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from mteb import MTEB"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "tasks = [\"ArguAna\", \"SciFact\", \"NFCorpus\"]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "evaluation = MTEB(tasks=tasks)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "results = evaluation.run(encoder, output_folder=\"./mteb-results\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Run your candidate models on a *representative* subset. Do not trust leaderboard rank alone \u2014 your domain matters."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: hand-rolled cosine from scratch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "See `code/main.py`. Averaged Hashing Trick embeddings (stdlib-only). Not competitive with transformer embeddings, but shows the shape: tokenize \u2192 vector \u2192 normalize \u2192 dot product."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy.** Encode 100 sentences with `bge-small-en-v1.5` at full dim (384), then at Matryoshka 128. Measure MRR drop on 10 queries.\n2. **Medium.** Compare BGE-M3 dense, sparse, and colbert on 500 passages from your domain. Which wins on recall@10? Does RRF fusion beat the best single mode?\n3. **Hard.** Run MTEB on three candidate models across your top-2 domain tasks. Report MTEB score, p99 latency on a 100-query batch, and $/1M queries. Pick the Pareto-optimal one."
      ]
    }
